{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":124415,"name":"Irit Katriel","username":"iritkatriel","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/iritkatriel/{size}/2615_2.png","created_at":"2023-11-01T13:57:13.901Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAt the last Language Summit in April, after three back to back sessions on the C API, we agreed that our discussions about the future of the C API are lacking a shared understanding of its current state, its strengths and weaknesses.  We decided to work towards a document summarising a community consensus on that, and have put together the draft of PEP 733.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0733/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/2X/8/88d4484552c4beac33d9a0848f523aaa66aad78c.png\" class=\"site-icon\" data-dominant-color=\"979F6B\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0733/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003epeps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0733/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ePEP 733 – An Evaluation of Python’s Public C API | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003ePython Enhancement Proposals (PEPs)\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIt is currently marked as draft and is open to amendments. As an informational PEP, it does not require SC approval; I propose that the future \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/\"\u003eC API Workgroup\u003c/a\u003e will decide when to mark it as Final.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2023-11-01T13:57:13.901Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":725,"reads":152,"readers_count":151,"score":3925.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":37618,"topic_slug":"pep-733-an-evaluation-of-python-s-public-c-api","display_username":"Irit Katriel","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0733/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 733 – An Evaluation of Python’s Public C API | peps.python.org","clicks":112},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0731/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 731 – C API Working Group Charter | peps.python.org","clicks":10}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":19}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":2481,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-733-an-evaluation-of-python-s-public-c-api/37618/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":19}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":19,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":124526,"name":"Alex Waygood","username":"AlexWaygood","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/alexwaygood/{size}/4722_2.png","created_at":"2023-11-01T21:38:17.703Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks, Irit, for the huge amount of work you put into coordinating this effort.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"